=head1 DESCRIPTION

This structure contains information about one I<delivery> in your
account.

A delivery is a connection between a logical I<delivery source> and a
logical I<delivery destination>.

For more information, see CreateDelivery
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatchLogs/latest/APIReference/API_CreateDelivery.html).

To update an existing delivery configuration, use
UpdateDeliveryConfiguration
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatchLogs/latest/APIReference/API_UpdateDeliveryConfiguration.html).

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 Arn => Str

The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that uniquely identifies this delivery.


=head2 DeliveryDestinationArn => Str

The ARN of the delivery destination that is associated with this
delivery.


=head2 DeliveryDestinationType => Str

Displays whether the delivery destination associated with this delivery
is CloudWatch Logs, Amazon S3, or Firehose.


=head2 DeliverySourceName => Str

The name of the delivery source that is associated with this delivery.


=head2 FieldDelimiter => Str

The field delimiter that is used between record fields when the final
output format of a delivery is in C<Plain>, C<W3C>, or C<Raw> format.


=head2 Id => Str

The unique ID that identifies this delivery in your account.


=head2 RecordFields => ArrayRef[Str|Undef]

The record fields used in this delivery.


=head2 S3DeliveryConfiguration => L<Paws::CloudWatchLogs::S3DeliveryConfiguration>

This structure contains delivery configurations that apply only when
the delivery destination resource is an S3 bucket.


=head2 Tags => L<Paws::CloudWatchLogs::Tags>

The tags that have been assigned to this delivery.



